{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295839-mage-concept","id":1295839,"title":"Mage Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-11T08:54:43-07:00","id":1295839,"title":"Mage Concept","content":"Hey everyone, I've never played mage before but have been kicking around a character that I wanna use on a chat site. But I'm clueless how to start building the character.<br /> <br /> He's going to be based on Nathan Explosion and use music(if thats even possible) as his focus(foci?). I havent figured out paradigm or tradition but basically everything has to rock. Heavy metal style. And the sicker his playing is the more powerful the magic.<br /> <br /> Is this doable? And what should i be aware of that most new players miss in their RPing a mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:14:49-07:00","id":1296156,"title":"","content":"While I know very little of this Nathan Explosion but yeah, it sounds doable.<br /> <br /> A few points:<br /> <br /> *I'm not sure what edition you're using but usually mages have more than one focus. If you're not allowed to have one single focus, you can divide different aspects of Metal into different foci. Like say: his deep death-voice being one focus, an instrument being other, the music itself (the songs) another, and so on.<br /> <br /> *In M20 and Revised there's a rule about using Skills to empower your magick. You first have to roll the Skill you use to play your music (Interpretation), and if the result it's good it lowers the difficluty of the spell. That sounds about right for the &quot;the sicker his playing is the more powerful the magic&quot; aspect. Other than that the power of the magick would still be largely dependant on luck. You can always narrate that if the magick was weak it's because the play wasn't brutal enough (regarless of the result of the Interpretation roll).<br /> <br /> *Ritual Magic rules may be of interest. A long concert allows to pile up magic to create greater effects. Also you really want to find other Metal loving mages for your band because they can sum their own power to the total effect in rituals. Mundanes also can add to the power in a ritual, but only in groups and they need to know what they're doing (they need to be involved in the magic).<br /> <br /> *Tradition:<br /> Probably Ecstatic because these value emotion, feeling, and all that. Something being &quot;metal enough&quot; may be valued as magick by the Cult. They deal a lot with concerts. Woodstock was, if not their doing, influenced by them. And they also deal a lot in drugs, sex, the stuff that often surrounds rock.<br /> <br /> Other traditions can also work but he would be more of an outlier.<br /> <br /> *Paradigm it's how you explain your supernatural power to alter reality. Maybe your rock it's so hard that breaks the illusion of reality, allowing the impossible to happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T10:34:16-07:00","id":1296174,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that. It helped a lot. And if his playing is good and his magic rolls weak, I'll just figure he isnt satisfied. Maybe he might break his guitar in that case.<br /> <br /> Now what about using an enchanted guitar?<br /> <br /> And Nathan is from a fictional band called dethklok. I'm not a metal fan by nature but this seems like a fun character to play haha. Flying around Zappin' people with his guitar. Maybe he has aspirations to become rock god along side other real gods. I have no idea whats possible in this venue so I may be in for some nasty surprises. <br /> <br /> Could any of the magic be coincidental?<br /> <br /> And what would be the best spheres?<br /> <br /> My only other problem is that I have revised but the site uses M20 i think. Do i need to buy it, or can I get by with revised?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also the site has disparates or maybe their independents and traditions. I'm going to read more about it, but which group would he be in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8150,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","user":"Talvas","date":". 03-12-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:28:57-07:00","id":1296187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now what about using an enchanted guitar?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wonder Background has you covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could any of the magic be coincidental? </div> </div> </div>To be coincidental it needs to pass as something that could happen. In general flying and zapping people it's not going to be coincidental.<br /> <br /> Flying can pass as a special effect in a concert, but turning people into ash with metal powered ligthining bolts it's not going to fly so easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what would be the best spheres? </div> </div> </div>That really depends on what you want to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Spheres that come to mind: Mind to entice and charm the audience and Forces(perhaps + Prime) to have power over sound, fly and throw those lightning bolts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My only other problem is that I have revised but the site uses M20 i think. Do i need to buy it, or can I get by with revised? </div> </div> </div>M20 it's different from Revised. Magic rolls can be different, there are a few changes in the Spheres, Focus it's <i>very </i>different, Paradox can be different...M20 it's full of dials, depending on the optional rules they use it can be more or less similar to Revised but in general I don't think that book it's going to be enough<br /> <br /> M20 it's a big book. Ask them if having the rule book it's necessary to play, and tell them that you have Revised perhaps they can brief you in the differences (may be few depending on the optional rules they use).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the site has disparates or maybe their independents and traditions. I'm going to read more about it, but which group would he be in? </div> </div> </div>Doesn't sound like a disparate. Independant he may be but I would recomend the Traditions. Cult of Ecstasy. Because you have Revised you can read 'bout them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2019, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:47:43-07:00","id":1296191,"title":"","content":"Thanks a ton. You covered everything brilliantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T13:42:01-07:00","id":1296783,"title":"","content":"I've seen Metalocalypse, so I am familiar with Mr. Explosion. Are you planning on taking the basic idea and making it more serious, or keeping him just as silly as the original? In a general sense you have the right to create any character you want, but I recommend running this by the storyteller and see if this character matches with the tone of the story he or she is planning to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T04:54:44-07:00","id":1297209,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice. They said it was fine, and I do plan on going a little more serious, a lil dumb of course and insisting on everything being metal. But without most of the jokes...<br /> <br /> But I am gonna double check now, and see what they expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:15:47-07:00","id":1297341,"title":"","content":"For Nathan Explosion, I definitely see him as a Traditionalist. For the Tradition, I'm thinking either Cult of Ecstasy, Verbana (who have a significant Metal subculture), or the Euthanatos (because of all the death). Depends on whether he does what he does because brutality is how he achieves ecstasy, because he's committed to the brutal aspects of life, or because he's committed to the brutal aspects of Death, respectively.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I can think of few more appropriate Paradox backlashes than randomly puking blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:00:16-07:00","id":1297955,"title":"","content":"Thanks again guys. Whats a good paradigm? it has to be from the M20 book.<br /> <br /> Also I made the guitar wonder use matter spheres. Any other good ideas for it before I submit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:17:08-07:00","id":1297972,"title":"","content":"Focus it's divided in 3 parts.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm </b>it's &quot;just&quot; how you think the world works in order to empower your magick. This is very broad and thus almost any Paradigm could be incorporated into Metal. It's more of a question of *why* your music it's powerful.<br /> <br /> As some examples I think may be appropiate:<br /> <br /> <i>Everything\u2019s an Illusion, Prison, or a Mistake.</i> If this is the case then your music <i>somehow </i>&quot;breaks trough&quot; the prision allowing you to transcend it's limitations and impose new or different laws over the universe.<br /> <br /> <i>Everything is Chaos </i>posits that nothing has inherent meaning. In this case your music imposes your will on the world because it has meaning to you, and perhaps to your fans.<br /> <br /> <i>Might is Right</i>if you see your music as a tool of domination. Your Metal imposes on the world because it's so frigging powerful<br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b> It's *how* you alter the world. Here's where we have to focus to make Metal important, we need a &quot;musical&quot; Practice. Note that you don't need to (and probably won't) have all the Asociated Abilities of a Practice...but you're most likely to focus on some of them. What is most important it's to chose a Practice that resonates with the instruments we want to use.<br /> <br /> I think these two could be appropiate (you can chose both, as you can combine up to 3 Practices):<br /> <br /> <i>Chaos Magick</i> it's all about personal intuition and interpretation, and it's often very subversive. You could easily make your music the thing that allows you to focus your will &quot;to spin energy into being&quot;. <b>Art </b>it's an asociated ability, and <i>anything </i>can be chosen as Instrument, so it's not restrictive<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Chaos Magick</u><br /> It\u2019s not what you think it is. Although the term \u201cchaos magic\u201d tends to be associated with demons and evil, occultists understand chaos magick as a postmodern and often improvisational Art. Like other mystic practices, it emphasizes knowledge, reflection, and other forms of self-improvement. This revolutionary inversion of traditional mystic disciplines, however, depends upon personal intuition and interpretation; individual freedom; a deliberately iconoclastic approach; and an often subversive use of pop-culture symbols, social behaviors, and improvised designs.<br /> Chaos magick spits in the face of established dogma. Often regarded by outsiders as a Left-Hand Path, it\u2019s a sex, drugs, and rock-n-roll sort of practice, raising and directing personal energy<br /> (that is, Quintessence) through extreme experiences. Obviously, this sort of thing appeals to Cultists of Ecstasy, whose more formal practices \u2013 Tantra, vision questing, ordeals, and crazy wisdom (see below) \u2013 have been integrated into the chaosmagick potpourri. Even that diverse culture, however, is too confining for many chaos practitioners, whose embrace of the Chaosphere \u2013 the whirling fractal of absolute existence \u2013 resists confinement in any form.<br /> Playful yet serious, each chaos-magick practice draws from the individual practitioner\u2019s experiences and desires. Depending upon the individual practitioner, it can integrate formalized ritual or involve spontaneous improvisation\u2026 or both, or neither. Flexibility and personal investment are innate elements of the practice as a whole, often connected to psychic thought forms called egregores: concepts given reality through extensive investment of psychic energy. (See the Instruments entry for Thought Forms, pp. 598-599.) Some folks use toys and Tarot cards, whereas others draw sigils, craft graphic novels, run raves, stage flash mobs, and concoct elaborate pranks on society at large. Eris, Bob, the Flying Spaghetti Monster\u2026 these deities supplant the classic divinities in a chaotic pantheon whose figureheads are less concerned with worship than with inversion. Each mage, then, is a vortex of potential whose Will spins energy into being. And if this sounds too abstract to be useful, then you\u2019re thinking about it too hard.<br /> <u>Associated Paradigms: </u>A Mechanistic Cosmos; A World of Gods and Monsters; Creation\u2019s Divine and Alive; Divine Order and Earthly Chaos; Everything is Chaos; Everything\u2019s an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake; Might is Right; One-Way Trip to Oblivion<br /> <u>Associated Abilities</u>: Art, Awareness, Carousing, Computer, Esoterica, Expression, Lucid Dreaming, Meditation, Pharmacopeia, Streetwise, Technology<br /> <u>Common Instruments:</u> Whatever works, so long as none of it becomes too stable or confining. </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Crazy Wisdom </i>it's a similar but more philosophical Practice. In this case rather than manifesting your will you're trying to break established concepts about what's possible, even your own. Again, it has <b>Art </b>as asociated ability and &quot;dance, drugs, music,ordeals, sex and sensuality, social domination, and voice&quot; sounds like it's on the ballpark of what you want to do<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Crazy Wisdom</u><br /> A mage who gets a little bit out of her head when performing magick might use what\u2019s often called the crazy wisdom practice: deliberately irrational activities that supposedly grant wisdom by<br /> shattering established concepts of what is and is not possible and real.<br /> Another sex, drugs, and rock-n-roll approach to magick, crazy wisdom often involves psychoactive entheogens, tranceinducing music, vision quests, risky ordeals, sexual excess, gender inversions, social misrule, mass ecstatic rituals, and solitary isolation in which the practitioner turns her own personal reality inside out and then ponders what that means. Although it\u2019s technically undisciplined by the standards of more rigid forms of magick, such behavior provides a potent tool for<br /> enlightenment\u2026 assuming it doesn\u2019t kill you first!<br /> Although its obvious adherents come from the Cult of Ecstasy, crazy wisdom has a long and respected history as part of shamanism, voodoo, witchcraft, and even certain High Ritual practices. The Order of Hermes has its own variation \u2013 the Antinomian Praxis \u2013 in which a mage smashes taboos, violates her own standards, and breaks through constraints to find what lies beyond them. Drawing strength from its obvious contradictions, crazy wisdom is dangerous, disruptive, often scary, and potentially lethal. That\u2019s kind of the point, though danger isn\u2019t always involved. Mystic contraries and genderqueers, who deliberately invert social expectations about identity and gender, practice a form of crazy wisdom on a social scale, fucking with people\u2019s preconceptions in order to show greater possibilities. This is the Trickster\u2019s Path, breaking on through like Jim Morrison in a mosh pit with Patti Smith, Br\u2019er Rabbit, the Cat in the Hat, and several buckets of paint.<br /> <u>Associated Paradigms:</u> A World of Gods and Monsters; Creation\u2019s Divine and Alive; Divine Order and Earthly Chaos; Everything is Chaos; Everything\u2019s an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake; It\u2019s All Good \u2013 Have Faith; One-Way Trip to Oblivion<br /> <u>Associated Abilities</u>: Art, Athletics, Carousing, Esoterica, Lucid Dreaming, Meditation, Pharmacopeia, Survival Common Instruments: Blood and body fluids, bones and remains, brain/ computer interface, dance, drugs, music, ordeals, sex and sensuality, social domination, thought forms, toys, tricks and illusions, voice </div> </div> </div><b>Instruments </b>it's what previous editions treat as Foci. It's the &quot;tools&quot; you use to perform your magic. You will need 7 instruments and thus I repeat this suggestion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're not allowed to have one single focus, you can divide different aspects of Metal into different foci. Like say: his deep death-voice being one focus, an instrument being other, the music itself (the songs) another, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for other suggestions, I understand that one of the characteristics of Mr. Explosion it's that he always speak in a very deep voice known as &quot;death growl&quot;. If Merits and Defects AND M20 Book of Secrets are allowed, there's a merit that can be used to represent that unusual trait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BoS p.37</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enchanting Feature (2 pt. Merit)<br /> Blessed with magnificent eyes, sleek hair, mighty biceps, preternatural grace, ripped abs, a dazzling smile, or some other standout physical feature, you can enchant people with the raw perfection of that feature. The feature in question doesn\u2019t need to be visually obvious, either; maybe you smell good, possess a seductive voice, move with animalistic allure, or enjoy some likewise wondrous physical asset. (Please be tasteful here, folks.) This Merit takes the place of related Physical Merits such as Enchanting Gaze, Soothing Voice, Graceful, and other potentially similar attributes. Story-wise, this Enchanting Feature becomes a standout part of your character\u2019s description. System-wise, you reduce the difficulty by -2 when your character deploys the feature in question as part of some social feat. If your mage employs his Enchanting Feature Merit as part of his magickal focus (see the Instruments entries for Eye Contact, Dance and Movement, Ordeals and Exertions, Sex and Sensuality, Social Domination, and Voice and Vocalizations in Mage 20, Chapter Ten), then you could count this Merit as a personalized unique /specialized instrument (as detailed in Mage 20, pp. 503 and 588). On the plus side, this allows you to reduce certain casting difficulties by -2 when the feature inquestion is specifically employed in the casting of an Effect. On<br /> the not-so-good side, this might get your mage\u2019s eyes gouged out, his face marred, his vocal cords cut, or\u2026 well, you get the picture\u2026 if a particularly ruthless enemy considers that feature<br /> to be \u201cthe focus of his power.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This one also seemed appropiate, altrough I don't know much of the series so maybe I'm wrong...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Physically Impressive (2 pt. Merit)<br /> You are one imposing sumbitch, not so much large as apparently dangerous no matter what mood you might be in at the time. This could be as obvious as scarring or an intimidating build, or as intangible as the proverbial \u201cair of menace.\u201d System-wise, the Merit adds two dice to all Social-Trait rolls that involve intimidating someone; story-wise, people find you unnerving \u2013 and quite possibly attractive in a dangerous way \u2013 even when you\u2019re not trying to be impressive. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T16:47:12-07:00","id":1298074,"title":"","content":"Further suggestion: Thanks to M20: Book of Secrets, we get a bunch of extra Practices to choose from when creating our Nathan Explosion-alike. Including the most relevant to this situation, Bardism. It's not all about plucking a lute and singing softly about fair maidens. It's ANY performative method of drawing out magic. In this case, you character believes they are so brutal and so talented, they can sing Reality into new forms...or bring about its ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T17:44:08-07:00","id":1298083,"title":"","content":"If you have access to the Vampire book Rites of Blood I'd look a &quot;Punk Sorcery&quot; and try to back date some of the concepts to Mage magic, it seems to have much of the right world view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:14:43-07:00","id":1300052,"title":"","content":"Thanks you guys, I haven't had a chance to read it til now. Enchanting Feature is banned in all venues but the others are great.<br /> <br /> I gave him high ritual, art, and the skill that lets you do magic as part of a show. And i'm gonna look into bardism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}